From: XR1710G local fixes
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: allow a target-specific hardware timeout default

Airoha EN7581 at 150 MHz can represent at most 28 seconds; request 20,
retaining the 5-second ping and the 30-second default on other targets.
Reference: Linux drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c max_timeout calculation.

--- a/watchdog.c
+++ b/watchdog.c
@@ -30,7 +30,11 @@
 
 static struct uloop_timeout wdt_timeout;
 static int wdt_fd = -1;
-static int wdt_drv_timeout = 30;
+#ifndef DEFAULT_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT
+#define DEFAULT_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT 30
+#endif
+
+static int wdt_drv_timeout = DEFAULT_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT;
 static int wdt_frequency = 5;
 static bool wdt_magicclose = false;
 
